# Project: BlogMarketFinancial
# Language: English (en-US)
# Direction: LTR

# Frontend Guidelines
## Structure and Style
- Use Vazirmatn font for all texts
- Follow shadcn/ui component structure
- Use RGB variables for colors:
  * Primary: rgb(var(--c-primary-600))
  * Text: rgb(var(--c-primary-900))
  * Background: rgb(var(--c-primary-50))
- Mobile-first responsive design
- Client components with 'use client'

## User Interface
- Minimal and clean design
- Shadow cards with mild hover effects
- Smooth animations for interactions
- Skeleton loading states
- Toast messages for notifications

## Typography
- Base size: 16px (1rem)
- Main heading: 24px (1.5rem)
- Subheading: 20px (1.25rem)
- Small text: 14px (0.875rem)
- Line spacing: 1.6

## Base Components
- Buttons: Primary (Blue), Secondary (Gray), Danger (Red)
- Forms: Real-time validation, Clear error messages
- Tables: Fixed header, Pagination, Sorting
- Modals: Soft animation, Close button

# Backend Guidelines
## Core Structure
- Follow Next.js 13+ App Router structure
- Use Prisma for database operations
- Business logic in actions folder
- Error management in API routes
- Log important operations

## File Structure
- /src/app/(site): Public pages
- /src/app/dashboard: Management panel
- /src/app/api: API endpoints
- /src/components: React components
- /src/actions: Server actions
- /src/lib: Utility functions
- /src/hooks: Custom hooks
- /src/types: TypeScript types
- /src/utils: General functions

## Component Structure
- Imports
- Type definitions
- Component definition
- State management
- Effects
- Helper functions
- JSX output

## API Response Format
{
  success: boolean
  data?: any
  message?: string
  errors?: { field?: string; message: string }[]
}

## Database Models
- Follow Prisma schema
- Proper relationships
- Soft delete implementation
- Organized migrations

## Authentication
- Use NextAuth.js
- Role-based access
- Protect sensitive routes
- Session management

## Error Management
- Use try/catch
- Appropriate error messages
- Error logging
- User-friendly message display

## State Management
- Use React hooks
- Context when necessary
- State close to usage point

## Performance
- Proper loading states
- Pagination
- Image optimization
- Appropriate caching

## Security
- Input validation
- Output sanitization
- CSRF protection
- Rate limiting

## Testing
- Unit tests for critical functions
- API endpoint tests
- E2E tests for critical processes

## Code Style
- Use TypeScript
- Follow ESLint rules
- Format with Prettier
- Meaningful comments